WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.899 --> 00:00:07.469
- Give me some room. I need
some room. Give me some space.

00:00:07.469 --> 00:00:08.704
- Oh my God.

00:00:08.704 --> 00:00:09.517
- What?

00:00:09.517 --> 00:00:11.385
- Adele just released a new song.

00:00:11.385 --> 00:00:13.220
- Oh no.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.925
- I remember the first time
I heard "Someone Like You",

00:00:15.925 --> 00:00:19.606
I cried for two hours.

00:00:19.946 --> 00:00:22.658
Adele's music is so relatable and sad.

00:00:22.658 --> 00:00:24.260
- Shh. Do you hear that?

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.437
(gasp)

00:00:28.509 --> 00:00:30.827
- My God, it's already happening.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.061
- Adele's music is too beautiful.

00:00:33.061 --> 00:00:35.544
- The song is spreading
all over the internet.

00:00:35.584 --> 00:00:39.146
(cries)

00:00:40.636 --> 00:00:41.887
- We've got to protect people from

00:00:41.887 --> 00:00:43.590
reflecting on their past heart breaks.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:44.923
- (beep) yeah.

00:00:47.922 --> 00:00:50.368
This is for making me
think about my ex-boyfriend

00:00:50.368 --> 00:00:52.698
every time I hear "Rolling in the Deep".

00:00:54.885 --> 00:00:56.575
- Whew. Hopefully nobody else here ah-

00:00:58.816 --> 00:01:00.840
- Like, you gotta listen to this.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.656
- No way. Her music is too emotional.

00:01:04.241 --> 00:01:08.274
(dramatic music)

00:01:09.857 --> 00:01:12.624
- Good job. Now let's
go save some more lives.

00:01:12.624 --> 00:01:14.302
(sobs)

00:01:14.302 --> 00:01:17.540
- Wait, sounds like
someone's sobbing in there.

00:01:23.194 --> 00:01:24.960
(louder sobs)

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.624
- My cat just died.

00:01:27.314 --> 00:01:28.898
- Oh, sorry about that.

00:01:32.408 --> 00:01:33.090
(gasp)

00:01:34.575 --> 00:01:36.399
- Alright, I'll rip off their
headphones, you go over-

00:01:36.399 --> 00:01:38.395
- Mike, we don't have
time to stop everyone

00:01:38.395 --> 00:01:39.617
from listening to Adele.

00:01:39.617 --> 00:01:40.839
We've gotta get outta here.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:46.063
(suspenseful music)

00:01:47.961 --> 00:01:49.274
- Kaitlyn, wait.

00:01:49.294 --> 00:01:50.655
- Why? What's wrong?

00:01:50.655 --> 00:01:52.664
- We can't run forever.

00:01:53.104 --> 00:01:55.322
Adele will never stop creating music

00:01:55.322 --> 00:01:57.362
that makes us feel naked and scarred

00:01:57.362 --> 00:01:59.868
and empowered, all at the same time.

00:02:00.198 --> 00:02:02.658
Whether it's today,
tomorrow, or next week,

00:02:02.658 --> 00:02:04.630
we're inevitably gonna hear her new song.

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:10.164
So let's face it, Adele can't be stopped.

00:02:21.831 --> 00:02:23.091
- [Voiceover] And in other news,

00:02:23.091 --> 00:02:25.960
the lack of rain in Los
Angeles is no longer a problem

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:28.947
thanks to all the tears
created by Adele's new song.

00:02:29.835 --> 00:02:34.642
(crying and sobbing)

